Modification: Gelasio matches the advance widths of Georgia but not its line
metrics, so each bundled face carries Georgia's vertical metrics instead of its
own. Outlines, advances, kerning and names are unchanged. With FontTools
4.66.1, for each face:

    font = TTFont(source, recalcBBoxes=False, recalcTimestamp=False)
    os2, hhea = font["OS/2"], font["hhea"]
    os2.usWinAscent, os2.usWinDescent = 1878, 449
    os2.sTypoAscender, os2.sTypoDescender, os2.sTypoLineGap = 1549, -444, 198
    os2.fsSelection &= ~(1 << 7)
    hhea.ascent, hhea.descent, hhea.lineGap = 1878, -449, 0
    font.save(output)

